# Every setting Echoturn reads, as a checklist rather than a second copy of the
# defaults. The values live in echoturn/config.py (the dial table) and in the
# adapters; nothing here has one, because two places holding "the default" is
# how one of them ends up wrong while both look right.
#
# Copy to .env and uncomment what you want. Blank counts as unset everywhere, so
# leaving a line as `ECHOTURN_TTS_PROVIDER=` means "use the default".

# --- providers ---------------------------------------------------------------
# mock (offline, the default), or openai for anything serving the OpenAI HTTP
# shape.
#ECHOTURN_LLM_PROVIDER=mock
#ECHOTURN_TTS_PROVIDER=mock
#ECHOTURN_ASR_PROVIDER=mock

# --- the OpenAI-compatible adapter -------------------------------------------
# The API root. Anything with the same routes works, which is what makes the
# adapter a protocol rather than a company.
#ECHOTURN_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
#ECHOTURN_LLM_MODEL=
#ECHOTURN_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=
#ECHOTURN_LLM_TIMEOUT=
#ECHOTURN_TTS_MODEL=
#ECHOTURN_TTS_VOICE=
#ECHOTURN_TTS_TIMEOUT=
#ECHOTURN_ASR_MODEL=
#ECHOTURN_ASR_TIMEOUT=

# --- the optional models -----------------------------------------------------
# Where the speech and endpointing models are looked for. They are not in the
# wheel, so this is a path rather than a package.
#ECHOTURN_MODEL_DIR=models

# --- what the demo tells the model it is -------------------------------------
# A host would use its own product's prompt; this is the terminal demo's.
#ECHOTURN_DEMO_SYSTEM=

# --- the turn-taking dials ---------------------------------------------------
# All twenty-two of them, in one table, in docs/tuning.md - each with what it
# was measured against. They are not repeated here on purpose: this file is the
# list of names, and that document is the explanation.
#
# ECHOTURN_ASR_SAMPLE_RATE      ECHOTURN_ASR_LANG            ECHOTURN_ASR_INCREMENTAL_MS
# ECHOTURN_VAD_ENGINE           ECHOTURN_SMART_TURN          ECHOTURN_VAD_END_MS
# ECHOTURN_VAD_END_CALL_MS      ECHOTURN_MIN_SPEECH_MS       ECHOTURN_REOPEN_MS
# ECHOTURN_SPECULATE_MS         ECHOTURN_SPECULATE_CALL_MS   ECHOTURN_BARGE_MS
# ECHOTURN_BARGE_FLOOR          ECHOTURN_BARGE_RATIO         ECHOTURN_TTS_FIRST_CHARS
# ECHOTURN_TTS_FIRST_MIN        ECHOTURN_TTS_CHUNK_CHARS     ECHOTURN_TTS_CHUNK_MIN
# ECHOTURN_TTS_FIRST_CALL_CHARS ECHOTURN_TTS_FIRST_CALL_MIN  ECHOTURN_TTS_POOL_SIZE
# ECHOTURN_IDLE_SPLIT_SEC

# --- the HTTP pool -----------------------------------------------------------
# Connections kept open for the API calls, process-wide.
#ECHOTURN_HTTP_POOL_SIZE=
